{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You have seen what I did to Egypt.</b> At the beginning of his mission he explains to them the matter of providence, which is the core principle of the Torah. For when the Holy One, blessed be He, destroys one nation for its sin and delivers another nation for its merit — this is among the proofs of providence and among the fundamental principles of punishment and reward. Therefore He said, אשר עשיתי למצרים — 'what I did to Egypt' — that I brought the plagues upon them and destroyed them in the sea, and you saw this with your own eyes; and with you, I delivered you from all those plagues in Egypt and at the sea. And this is what is said: ואשא אתכם על כנפי נשרים — 'and I bore you on eagles' wings' — that I protected you from troubles like an eagle that protects its young. And why He likened this to an eagle — our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: just as this eagle, the king of birds, is not afraid of a bird but only of an arrow; and all the other birds carry their young between their feet, because they are afraid of the bird above them, but this eagle carries them on its wings, as it is written (Deuteronomy 32:11): ״כנשר יעיר קנו על גוזליו ירחף״ — it says: better that the arrow enter me and not my children. So too Israel, when they went out of Egypt and came into the sea, the Egyptians were pursuing them, and the two pillars — the pillar of cloud and the pillar of fire — were separating between the camp of Egypt and the camp of Israel. And the Egyptians were casting arrows and catapult stones at Israel, and the pillar of cloud would receive them." "<b>And according to</b> this Midrash, it would have been fitting to say, ואשא אתכם על כנף נשר — 'and I bore you on an eagle's wing' — for the intention is to liken the belovedness of the Omnipresent to the belovedness of the eagle for its young, which carries them on its wings. And it is possible to say that He mentioned 'eagles' in the plural as an allusion to the two pillars, for from the hour they went out of Egypt — as Scripture said (Exodus 12:37): ויסעו בני ישראל מרעמסס סכותה — immediately the pillar of cloud was by day to guide them on the way and the pillar of fire by night to illuminate for them, and so it is written (Exodus 13:14): ויסע מלאך האלהים ויסע עמוד הענן מפניהם. And he said:"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:03.533227674Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}